  "intro": {
    "answerFirst": "Belgrade's street food scene offers delicious eats in the $1-10 range, with Pekara Trpković being a top recommendation for its burek. This guide, curated from Reddit reviews and local recommendations, explores the best of Belgrade's street food, perfect for any time of year.",
    "body": [
      "Belgrade sits at the crossroads of Ottoman, Austro-Hungarian, and Slavic culinary traditions &mdash; and nowhere is this more evident than in its street food. The Serbian capital's grill culture ( ro&#353;tilj ) is a religion unto itself: smoky pljeskavica patties, perfectly charred &#263;evapi, and impossibly creamy kajmak. Add 24-hour bakeries, bustling farmers' markets, and artisan ice cream, and you have one of Europe's most underrated food cities. A full feast rarely costs more than $7."
    ]
