  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is the most popular street food in Belgrade?",
      "answer": "Pljeskavica is Belgrade's most iconic street food — a grilled meat patty made from pork, beef, and lamb, served in a lepinja with kajmak, ajvar, or urnebes. The Leskovac-style pljeskavica is legally protected and considered the gold standard."
    },
    {
      "question": "Where can I find the best ćevapi in Belgrade?",
      "answer": "Ćevap kod Dekija in Dorćol is the consensus top pick. Walter on Strahinjića Bana is the most popular chain option with Bosnian-style ćevapi. Drama Ćevapi near Kalemegdan is a great casual spot."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is burek and where should I try it?",
      "answer": "Burek is a flaky phyllo pastry filled with meat, cheese, spinach, or potato. Pekara Trpković is the Reddit favorite. Burek Non-Stop Čubura is open 24/7. Lili M-Burek near Zeleni Venac is beloved by locals."
    },
    {
      "question": "How much does street food cost in Belgrade?",
      "answer": "Belgrade street food is exceptionally affordable. Pljeskavica costs 350-600 RSD ($3-5 USD), ćevapi runs 500-800 RSD ($4.50-7), and burek is 120-250 RSD ($1-2.20). A full meal rarely exceeds $7."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is Belgrade street food good for vegetarians?",
      "answer": "Serbian street food is meat-focused, but vegetarians have options: cheese/spinach/potato burek, palačinke (crepes), gibanica (cheese pastry), proja (cornbread), and fresh produce at Zeleni Venac market."
    },
    {
      "question": "What time do Belgrade street food spots open?",
      "answer": "Bakeries open at 6-7 AM. Grill spots open at 9-10 AM and run until midnight. Burek Non-Stop Čubura is open 24 hours. Late-night pljeskavica stands come alive after midnight."
    },
    {
      "question": "What should I order at a Belgrade grill restaurant?",
      "answer": "Start with gurmanska pljeskavica with ajvar. Add 10 ćevapi with kajmak and onions. Get urnebes and šopska salata as sides. Pair with Jelen or Zaječarsko beer. Total cost: under €10."
    }
  ],
